    "description": "MN8 Energy owns and operates utility-scale and distributed solar assets, battery storage systems, and EV-charging infrastructure across the United States. Its customers include corporate, industrial, and mobility users that procure renewable power, charging, and related infrastructure services under long-term contractual arrangements. The operating model is asset heavy and primarily contracted, with power and infrastructure cash flows supported by long-duration customer agreements rather than merchant-only exposure. Public company materials state that the platform has more than 3 gigawatts of operating solar generation, more than 250 megawatts of battery storage, over 800 projects, and a presence in more than 25 states. Ridgewood announced a structured equity investment in the company in 2024, with the form of capital described as preferred growth equity. The investment gives Ridgewood exposure to a scaled U.S. renewable and charging platform while leaving broader ownership details undisclosed.",
